  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0166 database is designed to manage various aspects of a retail business, including products, customers, employees, payments, and sales transactions. The database consists of 16 tables, each representing a distinct entity within the business. The BRAND table stores information about different brands, with a unique brand ID and name, as well as an optional email address. The COLOR table contains a list of available colors, identified by a six-character code and a descriptive name. The CATEGORY table categorizes products, with each category having a unique ID and name. The SIZE table lists available product sizes, with a two-character code and a description. The GENDER table stores information about product genders, with a unique ID and name. The TYPE table links products to categories, with a unique ID, name, and a foreign key referencing the CATEGORY table. The PRODUCT table stores detailed information about each product, including its ID, type, size, color, name, brand, gender, description, and prices. The EMPLOYEE and CUSTOMER tables store employee and customer information, respectively, with unique IDs, names, dates of birth, emails, and phone numbers. The CCPAYMENT_STATE table lists possible payment states, with a one-character code and description. The CCPAYMENT table manages payment transactions, with a unique ID, payment type, expected, approved, and actual amounts, as well as timestamps for creation, update, and expiration. The CCPAYMENT_TYPE table lists payment types, with a two-character code and description. The CCENTRY_METHOD table stores entry methods, with a one-character code and description. The CCPAYMENT_CARD table stores payment card information, with a unique payment ID, payment type, encryption status, card number, bank name, expiration date, and entry method. The TICKET table stores sales transactions, with a unique ID, timestamps, employee and customer IDs, total product, tax, and order amounts, as well as a foreign key referencing the CCPAYMENT table. The TICKET_ITEM table links sales transactions to products, with a unique ticket ID, sequence number, product ID, quantity, price, tax amount, and product amount.",
  "gold_question": "Small Fashion Shop \n\n 1) Background / Context\nA local fashion retailer is struggling with managing their inventory and gaining insights into customer preferences due to a lack of digital storage systems for inventory, sales, and payment data. This inefficiency impacts their ability to maintain competitiveness in the market.\n\n 2) Objectives\nThe primary objective is to develop a structured database system to store product, sales, and payment information. The system should allow for generation of business insights and recommendations by querying the database.\n\n 3) Stakeholders & Users\n- Stakeholders: \n  - Shop Owners: Interested in high-level business insights and sales performance.\n  - Managers: Need detailed inventory management and sales reporting.\n  \n- Users: \n  - Employees: Will interact with the system for transaction processing and inventory updates.\n  - Customers: Indirect users whose purchase data informs business insights.\n\n 4) Functional Descriptions\n- Database Design and Implementation:\n  - Create tables for storing brand, product, sales, payment, and customer data.\n  - Maintain relationships between entities (e.g., products and categories).\n  \n- Inventory Management:\n  - Track product details such as color, size, and brand.\n  - Update inventory based on sales transactions.\n  \n- Sales and Payment Processing:\n  - Record sales tickets, including employee and customer information, product details, and pricing.\n  - Handle credit card payment information, ensuring state and type are recorded.\n  \n- Business Insights and Reporting:\n  - Analyze data to identify top-selling products and customer preferences.\n  - Generate reports for sales performance and inventory status.\n\n 5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n- Performance: \n  - Efficient querying to quickly retrieve business insights.\n  - Capable of handling concurrent transactions without degradation.\n  \n- Security:\n  - Protect sensitive customer and payment information.\n  - Ensure compliance with data protection regulations.\n  \n- Scalability: \n  - Allow for future expansion to accommodate more products and customers.\n  \n- Usability:\n  - Provide user-friendly interfaces for employees to update and access information.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0166.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0166\nCREATE TABLE `brand` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `color` (\n  `code` char(6) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `category` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `size` (\n  `code` char(2) NOT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `gender` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `type` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `category_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `type_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`category_id`) REFERENCES `category` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `product` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `brand_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `gender_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `color_code` char(6) NOT NULL,\n  `size_code` char(2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `product_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`brand_id`) REFERENCES `brand` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `product_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`gender_id`) REFERENCES `gender` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `product_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`color_code`) REFERENCES `color` (`code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `product_ibfk_4` FOREIGN KEY (`size_code`) REFERENCES `size` (`code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `employee` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `dob` date NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `customer` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `dob` date NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `ccpayment_state` (\n  `code` char(1) NOT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `ccpayment` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `payment_type` char(2) NOT NULL,\n  `expected_amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `approved_amount` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `actual_amount` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `expires_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `ccpayment_type` (\n  `code` char(2) NOT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `ccentry_method` (\n  `code` char(1) NOT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `ccpayment_card` (\n  `payment_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `payment_type` char(2) NOT NULL,\n  `encryption_status` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `card_number` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `bank_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `expiration_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `entry_method` char(1) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`payment_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `ccpayment_card_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`payment_id`) REFERENCES `ccpayment` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `ccpayment_card_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`payment_type`) REFERENCES `ccpayment_type` (`code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `ccpayment_card_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`entry_method`) REFERENCES `ccentry_method` (`code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `ticket` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `total_product` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `tax` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `order_amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `payment_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `ticket_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`employee_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `ticket_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `ticket_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`payment_id`) REFERENCES `ccpayment` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `ticket_item` (\n  `ticket_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sequence_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `tax_amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `product_amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`ticket_id`, `sequence_number`),\n  CONSTRAINT `ticket_item_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`ticket_id`) REFERENCES `ticket` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `ticket_item_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `product` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
